{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "CASE \"Computer Aided Software Engineering\""}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to talk about Computer Aided Software Engineering."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations. Explain important features related to object programming in different contexts and with different types of object programming."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n4le01ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The First Conditional in Affirmative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <strong>first conditional</strong> to talk about things that are likely to happen in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>As with any other type of conditional, for the first conditional you need two clauses. Take a look at the following example:</p> <p><i>If you <strong>take</strong> the meds prescribed by the doctor, you <strong>will feel</strong> better.</i></p> <p>Notice that the first clause (condition) is written in the&nbsp;simple present, while the second one (result) is written in simple future. You have to use the following grammatical structure whenever you use the first conditional:&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">If + subject + verb (present simple) + complement + , + Subject + will/won&rsquo;t (simple future) + verb (base form) + complement</p> <p>However, the order of the clauses is not always the same. You can either place the <strong><i>if clause</i></strong> before or after the <strong><i>simple future clause</i></strong>:</p> <p><i>You <strong>will feel</strong> better if you <strong>take</strong> the meds prescribed by the doctor.*</i></p> <p>*Compare the two examples and notice that when you place the <i>if clause </i>after the sentence in simple future, there is no need of adding a comma in between.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If a group of software developers is starting a project and they use CASE tools, they'll increase the quality of the software. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If the teacher asks me about the golden age of these tools, I'll say that it was in the 90's. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If a group of software developers is starting a project and they use CASE tools, they'll increase the quality of the software. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Order of Adjectives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <strong>adjectives</strong> to make descriptions. When you place different adjectives before a noun, you need to follow certain rules."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>Take a look at the following example:</p> <p><i>What an <strong>essential</strong>, <strong>useful</strong>, <strong>multipurpose</strong> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">tool for software developers!</span></i></p> <p>Now, pay attention to this formula:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Determiner (<i>What an</i>) + Adjectives (<strong><i>essential, useful, multipurpose</i></strong>) + <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Noun (<i>tool for software</i>)</span></p> <p>Notice that there are three adjectives describing the noun. There is an inner logic in the order of adjectives, so whenever you want to use more than one adjective before a noun, you need to take the following order into account:</p>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Category\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Examples of adjectives \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1. Opinion\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Important, useful\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2. Size\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Big, small\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"3. Physical quality\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Tidy, Skinny\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"4. Shape\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Round, square\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"5. Age\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Young, old\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"6. Color\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Yellow, red\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"7. Origin\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Colombian,English,Spanish\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"8. Material\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Iron, plastic\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"9. Purpose\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Organizing, cleaning, structuring \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"10. Noun\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"House, tool, car\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>When using the <i>verb to be</i> before the adjectives, you can always add the conjunction <strong><i>and</i></strong><i>. </i>Let&rsquo;s see:</p> <p><i>CASE is a <strong>multipurpose</strong> and <strong>essential</strong> tool for code writers</i>.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "As you know, software developers usually work in complex, large, multipurpose project."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Let me ask you some important and sly questions. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "CASE comes in handy in those cases as it provides efficient and quick solutions aimed to save time."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "software life-cycle "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "it refers to the different stages of software development, which are: requirements analysis, design, implementation, verification and maintenance"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You need to use each tool in a different stage of the software life-cycle."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le01ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "synonym for tricky or sharp"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let me ask you some important and sly questions"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le01ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wink of sleep"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "short time of sleep"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I stayed up late reading, I couldn't get a wink of sleep because of it. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le01ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "in a nutshell "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "expression used when summarizing something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In a nutshell, CASE tools allow code writers, designers, and software developers to keep track of every stage in a project."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le01ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "handy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "synonym for useful "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: CASE comes in handy in those cases as it provides efficient and quick solutions aimed to save time."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le01ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fuse "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to gather or combine "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's an innovative way of fusing different and functional appliances."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le01ob08aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine you are in chart of apply the CASE tools correctly in your company. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think a way to explain your work-team how they work, their features and some examples."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a brochure in order to present correctly the topic, use graphics, images and tip words. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with your partners and make them some questions."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I think a way to explain your work-team how they work, their features and some examples. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I design a brochure in order to present correctly the CASE tools. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about CASE tools and their features."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe7n4le01ob08re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Mark</strong>: Did you study for the exam on CASE?</br>\n<strong>Steve</strong>: I stayed up late reading, I couldn't get a wink of sleep because of it. </br>\n<strong>Mark</strong>: Let me ask you some important and sly questions. What does it stand for? </br>\n<strong>Steve</strong>: It stands for Computer Aided Software Engineering and it's defined as a method or set of tools you can use in a software developing process.</br>\n<strong>Mark</strong>: What's the exact role of CASE in this process? </br>\n<strong>Steve</strong>: In a nutshell, CASE tools allow code writers, designers, and software developers to keep track of every stage in a project. As you know, software developers usually work in complex, large, multipurpose projects; CASE comes in handy in those cases as it provides efficient and quick solutions aimed to save time."}, {"time": "53500", "image": "enpe7n4le01ob08re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Mark</strong>: Could you give me an example? </br>\n<strong>Steve</strong>: If a group of software developers is starting a project and they use CASE tools, they'll increase the quality of the software. Besides, they'll also improve the software's productivity if they use the tools. People usually need them when working with large systems. Besides, they help in the stages of analysis and design of software. There is a three-category classification for these appliances: Point tools, Workbenches, and Environments; you need to use each tool in a different stage of the software life-cycle."}, {"time": "93900", "image": "enpe7n4le01ob08re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Mark</strong>: Why is CASE important? </br>\n<strong>Steve</strong>: It's an innovative way of fusing different and functional appliances. Thanks to these technological advances we can combine mechanisms to make a process easier. As you didn't ask me about CASE history, let me give you some facts about it. Excelerator was the first CASE application, and its creators released it in 1984.If the teacher asks me about the golden age of these tools, I'll say that it was in the 90's. However, I need to get more information on the role of CASE nowadays."}], "coverimg": "enpe7n4le01ob08re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n4le01ob08re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 3, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain what CASE is. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe important features related to CASE. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk briefly about the history of CASE."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you think the process of software development is? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you know any tools that help software designers and code writers organize and control the development of software? Which ones?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "CASE? What is it about?"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [3], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type"